FYI...

I'm experimenting with a new patchwork-bot kernel.org service[1] which
will automatically update the patchwork I use for tracking linux-amlogic
patches[2] when I push patches to my tree. it is also sending me summary
reports (like the one below) when it updates the patchwork status.

Also, it can optionally notify the submitter directly when their patches
are applied (see [1] for more details on the notification submitters
would receive.)

Since I'm an early adopter of this service, I've chosen for now to not
enable the "notify subscriber" option, but for those of you who are
submitting patches, would you want to get these automatic notifications
when your patches are merged into my tree?   Note that these
notifications are for when they merge into *my* tree, which means they
are queued for the next merge window, but not yet in arm-soc or
mainline.

Kevin


[1] https://korg.wiki.kernel.org/userdoc/patchwork
[2] https://patchwork.kernel.org/project/linux-amlogic/list/


